(vector (map (:db/id -1), (:adr/id "2607242600"), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-lei-* -- ToSMonitor-LLM/ToSArchiveGovernor actor, round 5: extend from 41 to 51 of ~155 repos, self-paced /loop continuation"), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/date "2026-07-24"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/related (vector "90-docs/adr/2607241900-cloud-itonami-lei-tos-monitor-actor-pilot.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607242000-cloud-itonami-lei-tos-monitor-actor-batch10.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607242300-cloud-itonami-lei-tos-monitor-actor-batch10-round2.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607242400-cloud-itonami-lei-tos-monitor-actor-batch10-round3.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607242500-cloud-itonami-lei-tos-monitor-actor-batch10-round4.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607110300-cloud-itonami-lei-corporate-tos-catalog.edn")), (:adr/scope-still-not-fleet-wide "this ADR extends the actor layer to 10 MORE cloud-itonami-lei-* repos (51 of ~155 total after this round). ~104 repos remain untouched, governed solely by ADR-2607110300. This is the second round dispatched automatically by the self-paced /loop set up during round 3 (ADR-2607242400), following round 4 (ADR-2607242500) -- no fresh owner request triggered this round, the round-3 request to establish the loop continues to authorize it"), (:adr/batch-companies "cloud-itonami-lei-2138004kw8bv57iii342 (Publicis Groupe SA, FR -- first :legal-notice doc-type company sampled in this actor family), cloud-itonami-lei-254900em62y5rrtj9771 (SBS Transit Ltd, Singapore -- first SG-jurisdiction company), cloud-itonami-lei-5299003fu7v4i45fu310 (KDDI Corporation, JP -- second JP company after TEPCO, first :privacy-policy doc-type sampled from Japan), cloud-itonami-lei-529900pm64wh8af1e917 (BASF SE, DE), cloud-itonami-lei-549300btns7mhshrlr55 (Par Pacific Holdings Inc, US-DE), cloud-itonami-lei-549300i2pvfbc9mfac61 (Teladoc Health Inc, US-DE), cloud-itonami-lei-549300siv6fps9y7ih33 (T. Rowe Price Group Inc, US-MD), cloud-itonami-lei-7245009eaauuqj0u4t57 (Randstad N.V., NL), cloud-itonami-lei-98tptum4ivmfczbcur27 (Enbridge Inc, Canada), cloud-itonami-lei-k2neh8qnvw44jiwk7z55 (Royal Caribbean Cruises Ltd, Liberia -- first LR-jurisdiction/flag-of-convenience company) -- evenly-spread sample (every ~11th repo) of the remaining pool (114 repos after round 4), not cherry-picked"), (:adr/parallel-subagent-construction "same construction method as rounds 3-4: one independently-dispatched Agent-tool subagent per company, self-contained prompt with pre-read real archive metadata (blueprint.edn + tos.journal.edn, extracted by the orchestrating session via grep/python3 field extraction rather than reading full journal text into context), the required lint/test bar, and the exact git workflow"), (:adr/identical-code-per-company "tosmonitor.governor/phase/operation/registry/advisor remain byte-identical across all 51 repos now carrying this actor -- fifth consecutive round with zero further template code changes needed, following round 1's two real fixes"), (:adr/test-status-batch10-round5 "each of the 10 repos independently passes its own governor contract (6 HARD checks + high-stakes/never-auto invariant), phase invariants, store parity (MemStore/DatomicStore), and advisor smoke tests before commit"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607242600: cloud-itonami-lei-* ToSMonitor round-5 batch-of-10, self-paced /loop continuation\n\n- Status: Accepted (2026-07-24)\n- Related: ADR-2607241900 (pilot); ADR-2607242000/ADR-2607242300/ADR-2607242400/ADR-2607242500 (rounds 1-4);\n  ADR-2607110300 (archive-only design still governing the other ~104 repos).\n\n## Context\n\nRound 4 (ADR-2607242500) was the self-paced `/loop`'s first automatic re-firing\nafter the owner set up the continuation mechanism during round 3. This ADR\nrecords the loop's second automatic re-firing, again with no new owner message\nrequesting this specific round -- the round-3 request to establish the loop is\nwhat continues to authorize it. Round 4 confirmed the fourth consecutive round\nwith zero template code changes needed; this round extends that streak to five.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **10 more repos** (51 of ~155 total), evenly sampled from the remaining pool\n   of 114. Two new jurisdiction firsts: SBS Transit Ltd (Singapore) and Royal\n   Caribbean Cruises Ltd (Liberia, a flag-of-convenience registration for a\n   cruise line headquartered/operating from Florida -- notable because the\n   `:company/jurisdiction` field reflects legal domicile, not operational\n   headquarters). Also the first sampled `:legal-notice` doc-type company\n   (Publicis Groupe) since that keyword was added to `known-doc-types` during\n   round 1's vocabulary-survey fix.\n2. **Same parallel-subagent construction method as rounds 3-4.** One company\n   per independently-dispatched Agent-tool subagent, same self-contained\n   prompt pattern, same lint/test bar (0 errors, 25/70 tests), same git\n   workflow (branch, PR via explicit `--head`/`--base`, merge, return to\n   main). Real archive metadata was extracted via targeted grep/python3 field\n   parsing (source-url/retrieved-at/doc-type/entity-id) rather than reading\n   each journal's full archived page text into context, since several of\n   this round's archived texts are long (e.g. Publicis Groupe's French-\n   language mentions-legales page) and only the structured fields are needed\n   for the actor's demo-baseline provenance.\n3. **No further template changes.** Fifth consecutive round with the\n   byte-identical `governor`/`phase`/`operation`/`registry`/`advisor` files\n   requiring zero edits -- round 1's two fixes (domain-matching base-domain\n   heuristic, doc-type vocabulary) remain the only code changes across 51\n   repos and counting.\n4. **Still not fleet-wide.** ~104 `cloud-itonami-lei-*` repos remain\n   untouched, governed solely by ADR-2607110300. The loop re-evaluates after\n   each round whether to continue, per its own dynamic self-pacing logic --\n   this ADR does not itself commit to any further number of rounds.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- (+) Second consecutive fully-unattended round via the self-paced loop,\n  demonstrating the continuation mechanism working across multiple firings\n  as designed in round 3.\n- (+) Further validates the template against two more jurisdiction firsts\n  (Singapore, Liberia/flag-of-convenience) and the first sampled\n  `:legal-notice` doc-type company, with zero code changes needed.\n- (-) Same standing question every prior round's ADR has flagged, now\n  compounding: an unattended loop firing a second time without a human\n  re-confirming scope makes the eventual stopping-point decision (currently\n  51/155, one third of the way) more consequential the longer it runs\n  unexamined. This ADR does not resolve that question -- it remains an\n  explicit further decision, and the owner should be able to redirect or\n  stop the loop at any time.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607241900, ADR-2607242000, ADR-2607242300, ADR-2607242400,\n  ADR-2607242500, ADR-2607110300, ADR-2607199960 (the `/loop` continuation\n  precedent for this catalog family)\n- The 10 repos' own `docs/adr/0001-tos-monitor-actor.md` records\n")))
